<title>CANADA: Northern Telecom wins wireless contract.</title>
<headline>Northern Telecom wins wireless contract.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Telecom Ltd said on Thursday it won a three-year supply deal, expected to be worth roughly C$270 million, to supply NorTel equipment for Mobility Canada's 800 MHz cellular network.</p>
<p>The company said its platform will allow Mobility Canada to offer advanced voice and data services complementary to services being proposed for PCS.</p>
<p>Mobility Canada is made up of the wireless affiliates of the provincial wireline telephone companies.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
